 "workCards": {
  "regression": [
   "It passed in at least two earlier rounds and fails now: a change of ours broke it. Run `lc.py diag reg {ref}` and read its requests, responses and rule steps.",
   "Find the change: `git diff HEAD -- Modules/Core` and `git log -p -5 -- Modules/Core/BookSource Modules/Core/RuleEngine`.",
   "Fix the cause in the shared pipeline, never with a per-source condition. Add a unit test that fails without the fix.",
   "`lc.py verify {id} --tests 'yuedu appTests/<TestClass>'`; on GATE PASS, `lc.py done {id}`."
  ],
  "bridge-gap": [
   "The signature names a Java, jsoup or Legado API that our JavaScript runtime lacks or answers differently. Read Legado's code for it: grep legado-E/ first, then legado-md3/ (both in the repo root).",
   "Write the smallest case that shows Legado's behaviour in scripts/legado-compat/oracle/cases/<name>.json and run `lc.py oracle scripts/legado-compat/oracle/cases/<name>.json`. Its output is the expected value. Never guess a value.",
   "Implement it in the runtime (Modules/Core/RuleEngine/ModernParser/JS/) for every source alike: no source names, no URL checks, no fallback.",
   "Add a unit test whose expected values are the oracle's output, with the case name in a comment.",
   "`lc.py verify {id} --tests 'yuedu appTests/<TestClass>'`; on GATE PASS, `lc.py done {id}`.",
   "If the oracle fails the same way (Legado has the same error), `lc.py reject {id} --legado '<file:line, why it fails there too>'`."
  ],
  "js-error": [
   "Run `lc.py diag js {ref}`. Find the request whose response the failing script reads, and what came back.",
   "If our request is what the rule asks for (URL, method, body, headers, charset) and the site sent an error page, no data, or a changed format: `lc.py evidence add {ref} --kind site --diag js --proof '<what the response shows>' --legado '<the code path where Legado gets the same response and fails>'`.",
   "If our runtime evaluated something differently from Rhino or jsoup (check with lc.py oracle): `lc.py add bridge:<short-name> --sources {ref} --controls '<regex for sources using the same API>' --why '<oracle case and result>'`, then `lc.py next`.",
   "If neither: `lc.py block {id} --reason '<what you saw>'`."
  ],
  "empty": [
   "Run `lc.py diag empty {ref}` and `lc.py src {ref}`. Compare the rule with the HTML the site sent.",
   "Check the rule against the saved HTML with jsoup through lc.py oracle (html + doc.select(...)).",
   "jsoup selects nothing either: the site changed. `lc.py evidence add {ref} --kind source --diag empty --proof '...' --legado '...'`.",
   "jsoup selects something but we did not: our parser differs. `lc.py add bridge:<short-name> --sources {ref} --controls '<regex>' --why '...'`, then `lc.py next`.",
   "Neither: `lc.py block {id} --reason '...'`."
  ],
  "http-error": [
   "Run `lc.py diag http {ref}`. Check that our request equals what the rule specifies: URL, method, body, headers, charset.",
   "Same request and the site answers 4xx or 5xx: `lc.py evidence add {ref} --kind site --diag http --proof '<status, URL, body head>' --legado '<Legado sends the same request: where>'`.",
   "Our request differs: it is an engine gap. `lc.py add bridge:<request-feature> --sources {ref} --controls '<regex>' --why '...'`, then `lc.py next`."
  ],
  "antibot": [
   "Run `lc.py diag antibot {ref}`. Never try to get past a verification page, challenge or WAF.",
   "A verification or challenge page that the source has no login or check for: `lc.py evidence add {ref} --kind antibot --diag antibot --proof '<page title, status>' --legado '<Legado gets the same page>'`.",
   "Otherwise treat it as js-error (step 3 of that card)."
  ],
  "interaction": [
   "The source asked for a captcha, a login or a browser page, which the audit cancels. Run `lc.py diag ui {ref}`.",
   "A person must log in or solve a captcha: `lc.py evidence add {ref} --kind login --diag ui --proof '...' --legado '<Legado shows the same prompt>'`.",
   "Legado would load that page by itself in a background WebView: `lc.py add bridge:<short-name> --sources {ref} --controls '<regex>' --why '...'`."
  ],
  "network": [
   "The request timed out or the connection failed, though the probe reached the origin. Run `lc.py diag net {ref}` once.",
   "It loads now: network noise. `lc.py skip {id} --reason 'loaded in diag net'`.",
   "It fails again on a host the probe did not test (an API or CDN host): `lc.py evidence add {ref} --kind site --diag net --proof '<host, error>' --legado '<same host, same request>'`."
  ],
  "unknown": [
   "Run `lc.py diag unknown {ref}`, describe what failed, and follow the card of the class it turns out to be.",
   "If no card fits: `lc.py block {id} --reason '<what you saw>'`."
  ]
 },
